<time datetime="2023-02-06">February 6, 2023</time>
<article id="BOINC" class="WebBits">
    <h2>TRY: Searching for pulsars</h2>
    <figure class="imgShadow pictureCaption">
        <a class="pswp-gallery__item" href="../library/img/boinc_project.webp" data-pswp-width="420"
           data-pswp-height="400">
            <img class="bitsImage imgShadow" src="../library/img/boinc_project.webp"
                 alt="einstein@home project example">
        </a>
    </figure>
    <p>
        SETI@home is well known in the astronomy community. The project is no
        longer collecting new data, however, data revision continues today.
        SETI@home <i><strong>(not imaged)</strong></i> and other projects
        operate similarly using
        <a href="https://boinc.berkeley.edu/" rel="external noopener" target="_blank" title="BOINC">
            Berkely Open Infrastructure
            for Network Computing (BOINC)
        </a>.
    </p>

    <p>
        Einstein@home calculates radio astronomy sets in search of new pulsars
        in our galaxy.
    </p>
    <aside class="examplePink">
        <p>Let science take over your computer:</p>
        <h4>Procedure:</h4>
        <ol id="BOINC-links">
            <li>
                <a href="https://scienceunited.org/" rel="external noopener" target="_blank" title="Science United">
                    Compute for
                    Science
                </a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://scienceunited.org/su_about.php" rel="external noopener" target="_blank"
                   title="About Science United">Learn about Science United</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://www.nsf.gov/news/special_reports/btyb/innovation.jsp" rel="external noopener" target="_blank"
                   title="Brought to You by NSF | National Science Foundation">
                    12 irreplaceable innovations made possible
                    by
                    NSF #The
                    Internet
                </a>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </aside>
</article>
